{"question_id": "8a2466db", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on your interest in learning more about video editing—particularly advanced settings in Adobe Premiere Pro—here are some resources I'd recommend:\n\n- **Official Adobe documentation and tutorials** — great for learning advanced features and settings directly from the source.\n- **YouTube channels**: Premiere Bro, Video Copilot, and Adobe Creative Cloud's channel — all excellent for visual, step-by-step tutorials (including color grading with the Lumetri Color Panel).\n- **Online courses**: Udemy, LinkedIn Learning, and Skillshare offer structured courses on Premiere Pro, including advanced and color grading topics.\n- **Communities**: r/premierepro on Reddit and Adobe's official forums — good places to ask questions and see how others solve editing problems.\n\nGiven you're still getting the hang of color grading, I'd especially suggest starting with Lumetri-focused tutorials on YouTube before moving to a full course.", "n_records": 5, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1706, "completion_tokens": 872, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|video_editing_software", "self|learning_goal", "self|color_grading_skill", "self|color_grading_tool_preference", "assistant|premiere_pro_learning_resources"], "digest_bytes": 754}
