{"question_id": "1a1907b4", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on your profile, here are tailored suggestions for your get-together:\n\n**Top pick: Pimm's Cup with a Twist** — You already liked the idea of this one, and you've made all the supporting choices: Ruby Red grapefruit simple syrup for depth, muddled cucumber slices, and a Collins glass to show off the color layers and garnishes. Since you're experimenting with new cocktails this weekend, this is the natural one to debut. (Recipe: 1.5 oz Hendrick's gin, 0.5 oz lemon juice, 0.5 oz simple syrup, 0.5 oz Pimm's No. 1, splash of ginger beer.)\n\n**Crowd-friendly alternatives featuring Hendrick's:**\n- **Rose Petal Spritz** — 2 oz Hendrick's gin, 2 oz Prosecco, 1 oz rose syrup, 1 oz lemon-lime soda. Effervescent and floral, great for a party.\n- **Gin-Gin Mule** — 2 oz Hendrick's gin, 4 oz ginger beer, squeeze of lime. Simple to batch for a group.\n- **Summer Solstice** — 2 oz Hendrick's gin, 1 oz peach puree, 1 oz lemon juice, 0.5 oz honey syrup. Seasonal and crowd-pleasing.\n\n**Presentation tip:** Use large clear ice cubes or spheres and garnish picks — you were already planning to experiment with garnishes (cucumber wheel, grapefruit slice, mint sprig, edible flowers), which will make whatever you serve look elegant.", "n_records": 31, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 3938, "completion_tokens": 1279, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|cocktail_experiment_plan", "self|gin_preference", "self|cocktails_made_before", "self|mixology_class_attended", "self|cocktail_choice", "self|cucumber_technique_choice", "self|simple_syrup_flavor_plan", "self|simple_syrup_choice", "self|grapefruit_variety_choice", "self|garnish_plan", "self|serving_glass_choice", "assistant|cocktail_recipe_pimms_cup_twist", "assistant|cocktail_recipe_cucumber_gimlet", "assistant|cocktail_recipe_rose_petal_spritz", "assistant|cocktail_recipe_gin_gin_mule", "assistant|cocktail_recipe_summer_solstice", "assistant|cocktail_reci