{"question_id": "57f827a0", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on your mid-century modern taste, here are some arrangement tips for this weekend:\n\n- **Make the dresser a focal point.** Your walnut piece with brass knobs is meant to be noticed — place it where the wood grain catches natural light, and keep the wall above it simple so it doesn't compete.\n- **Give pieces breathing room.** MCM furniture has low profiles and tapered legs that read best with open floor space around them. Pull pieces slightly off the wall rather than crowding them.\n- **Keep sight lines clean.** The aesthetic is about uncluttered lines — position the bed and dresser so you can see the legs and the floor beneath them, which keeps the room feeling light.\n- **Anchor with a rug.** A simple rug grounding the bed will tie the wood tones together without adding visual noise.\n- **Let function lead.** Mid-century modern is as much about practicality as looks — make sure the dresser drawers and closet path stay easy to access.\n- **Keep accents bold but minimal.** A single statement piece (a lamp, mirror, or plant) near the dresser will echo the era's \"bold accents\" without cluttering the space.", "n_records": 21, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 2800, "completion_tokens": 945, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|dresser_project", "self|dresser_replacement", "self|design_style_preference", "self|dresser_wood", "self|dresser_stain", "self|dresser_finish", "self|dresser_hardware", "self|hardware_rationale", "self|inspiration_search_plan", "assistant|recommended_furniture_retailers", "assistant|recommended_designers", "assistant|recommended_design_resources", "assistant|mcm_dresser_elements", "assistant|recommended_wood_types", "assistant|recommended_finishes", "assistant|finish_recommendation", "assistant|recommended_hardware_options", "assistant|recommended_hardware_brands", "assistant|recommended_design_blogs", "assistant|recommended_design_websites", "assistant|recommende